{"thought":"Looking at the current failure, the issue is that when all postings are cancelled, the result is an empty dict {} instead of {'cash': 0}. The test expects that accounts with cancelled postings should still appear with a zero balance. I need to ensure that accounts are included in the result even when their net balance is zero.

The problem is in my current implementation - I only add accounts to the totals dict when I process non-cancelled postings. But if all postings for an account are cancelled, the account never gets added to the totals dict.

I need to modify the logic to:
1. Track all accounts that have any postings (cancelled or not)
2. Ensure these accounts appear in the final result with their net balance (which could be zero)

